      "description": [
        {
          "text": "This family of proteins includes non-catalytic subunits of polygalacturonase as well as proteins containing a BURP domain at the C-terminus. Members of this family are involved in the regulation of plant cell size and growth, with some acting as chaperones for other proteins through the secretory pathway. The BURP domain is unique to plant proteins and plays a critical role in the function of these proteins, although the exact mechanisms are not fully understood.",
